Git and GitHub – Project Management
Why Git and GitHub?
Git:
A version control system.
Tracks changes in project files.
Helps manage daily work efficiently.
GitHub:
A cloud platform to store Git repositories.
Enables collaboration and project backup.
Used to submit daily internship tasks.

Branches in GitHub
Definition:
A branch is an independent line of development.
Why Branches Are Used:
To work on new features safely.
To avoid disturbing the main project.
To experiment without risk.
To enable team collaboration.
Main Branch:
Contains stable and final code.


Common Git Commands Used
git clone https://github.com/username/repo_name.git
cd <repo_name>
git add .
git commit -m "message"
git push origin main


Topic 2: Inheritance 
What is Inheritance?
Definition:
Inheritance is a mechanism in which one class acquires the properties and methods of another class.
The existing class is called the Parent Class.
The new class is called the Child Class.
Promotes code reusability.
Reduces redundancy.

Why Inheritance is Used
Reuse existing code.
Improve maintainability.
Represent real-world relationships.
Support extensibility.

Types of Inheritance in Python
Single Inheritance
One parent and one child class.
Multilevel Inheritance
A class derived from another derived class.
Hierarchical Inheritance
Multiple child classes inherit from one parent class.
Multiple Inheritance
One child class inherits from multiple parent classes.
Hybrid Inheritance
Combination of more than one type of inheritance.

Real-World Example Explanation
Parent Class: SocialMediaPost
Child Class: InstagramPost
InstagramPost automatically gets common behaviors and adds its own features.
